{
  "level": "Year 7",
  "subject": "selective",
  "title": "Powerful vocabulary and sentences",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "Same idea, more alive",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Two students can have the same idea. One sounds flat, one sounds alive."
        },
        {
          "say": "The difference is usually word choice and sentence shape.",
          "write": "words + sentences"
        },
        {
          "say": "Markers reward precise words and varied sentences.",
          "write": "precise · varied"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Verbs do the heavy lifting",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The exhausted hiker walked slowly up the last hill.",
          "write": "walked slowly"
        },
        {
          "say": "We need slow, heavy, tired movement. Sprinted is too fast. Skipped is too happy.",
          "write": "✗ sprinted  ✗ skipped"
        },
        {
          "say": "Trudged means walked slowly and heavily. One word does the job of two.",
          "write": "trudged",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 160,
            "alt": "walked slowly replaced by trudged",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 90,
                "text": "The hiker",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 123.00000000000001,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 173,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "walked slowly",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 123.00000000000001,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 173,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "trudged",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 306.0,
                "y": 90,
                "text": "up the hill.",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Precise nouns too. A car becomes a dented ute.",
          "write": "a car → a dented ute"
        },
        {
          "say": "Very is a warning light. Very big becomes huge or towering.",
          "write": "very big → towering"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Shade of meaning",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Words that look alike in a thesaurus can feel different."
        },
        {
          "say": "Famous is positive. Notorious means famous for something bad.",
          "write": "famous ≠ notorious",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 180,
            "alt": "Thin, skinny and slender on a feeling scale",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "x2": 520,
                "y2": 60,
                "color": "grey"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 40,
                "text": "negative",
                "size": 16,
                "color": "red",
                "anchor": "start",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 520,
                "y": 40,
                "text": "positive",
                "size": 16,
                "color": "green",
                "anchor": "end",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "red",
                "label": "skinny"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 210,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "thin"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 380,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 140,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "slender",
                "change": "highlight"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Thin is neutral. Skinny can be negative. Slender is positive.",
          "write": "skinny · thin · slender"
        },
        {
          "say": "Only use a word if you are sure of its meaning and feeling."
        }
      ]
    },
